  "published": "2026-06-30T13:20:30.207Z",
  "readmeFile": "readme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v.2.1.16\n    - Added MDK04 warnings for runtime references to source-defined attribute types trimmed during packing.\n\nv.2.1.15\n- Fixed: Separator bug where Mdk-IgnorePaths only accepted '|' but props files used ';'\n- Fixed: Analyzers now read ignore patterns directly from mdk.ini and mdk.local.ini files\n- Changed: ini files are now exposed as AdditionalFiles to analyzers\n- Improved: Ignore path separators now accept ';', '|', and ',' for maximum compatibility\n\n2.1.14\n    - Whitelist update\n\nv.2.1.12\n    - Fixed broken whitelist\n    \nv.2.1.11\n    - Whitelist update\n\nv.2.1.10\n    - Whitelist update... sorry about that\n\nv.2.1.9\n    - Package was not defined as a development dependency\n\nv.2.1.8\n    - SE 1.204 Update\n\nv.2.1.7\n - Fixed harmless warnings\n\nv.2.1.4\n - Legal crap, version parity\n\nv.2.1.3\n - _Someone_ left in a debugger call...\n\nv.2.1.2\n - New whitelist cache was actually _not_ embedded...\n - Fixed <Mdk-IgnorePaths> not actually working for multipaths because ; is a reserved character\n\nV.2.1.1\n - Fixed bad default ignore path \n\nV.2.1.0\n - Nuget Rename (I am _so_ sorry, it had to be done, won't happen again, I promise)\n - Added support for <Mdk-IgnorePaths> (see readme for instructions)\n - Updated whitelist cache",
